\section{Methods and custom architecture}
Baselines were climatology, persistence, and the recent six-row mean.
LightGBM ran once per feature arm. MLP, the existing Strata-OT Surface, and
Strata-OT Horizon v1 ran for seeds 17 and 41 on both arms.

Horizon v1 has separate endogenous and exogenous branches. History uses
levels, first differences, and cadence; weather uses levels, first
differences, and circular wind. Width-192 gated causal blocks use dilations
1 and 2. Fourier forecast-minute queries attend separately to the two
branches through six heads. The existing four-expert regime router fuses the
streams. Its point forecast is
\[
\widehat y=y_{\mathrm{last}}+\Delta_{\mathrm{history}}+
\sigma(g_{\mathrm{weather}})\Delta_{\mathrm{weather}}.
\]
The last term is exactly zero in the history-only arm. The existing Gaussian
scale and 0.10/0.50/0.90 quantile head are retained. All residual components,
weather gates, attentions, and regime weights are recorded. The measured
Horizon v1 parameter count is \VAR{summary.runs|selectattr("model", "equalto", "strata_ot_horizon")|map(attribute="parameters")|first|latex}.

\subsection{Exact training policy}
All neural runs used BF16 mixed precision, at most 80 epochs, selection-only
early stopping with patience 12, AdamW learning rate \(3\times10^{-4}\),
weight decay 0.01, one process, zero data workers, and four CPU threads.
Calibration was a validation-only scalar scale factor. No architecture,
horizon, feature, or success-rule retuning was allowed after assessment.

